## The organizing principle — define before you build, compose don't reinvent

Two **core** roles drive the pipeline (`product-designer`, `ui-designer`), plus three **supporting**
roles — `art-director` (creative direction), `flow-reviewer` (independent review), `consumer-migrator`
(migration) — with `data-analyst` running the empirical loop. Each owns a distinct **write-surface** and
**moment in the pipeline**, so they never collide.

| Role | Write surface | Owns (object type) |
|---|---|---|
| `product-designer` | SPECS only (markdown/docs, FigJam-level flow diagrams) | INTAKE — deconstruct the ask into business goal · metric · segment · JTBD · constraints · scope · CX success criteria · then flows · IA · journeys · state matrices · interaction + a11y behavior specs · acceptance criteria · functional microcopy · owns the usability-validation gate |
| `art-director` *(optional)* | `Explorations / <flow>` low-fi frames in the consumer file (quarantined from delivery) | CREATIVE DIRECTION — deconstruct a reference/trend → filter through the token/brand fence → adapt-not-copy → 2–3 named directions → build spec for `ui-designer` (runs the `visual-craft` canon) |
| `ui-designer` | CONSUMER Figma file `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}` (screen frames, layout, composition, states) | pixel-perfect, system-compliant screens composed from {{SYSTEM_NAME}} · build-time design-review self-check · consumer drift sweeps |
| `flow-reviewer` | read-only (review output) | INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation of screens + flows — runs the `ux-flow-review` canon; the expert-review gate |
| `data-analyst` | read-only (analysis output) | EMPIRICAL validation — turns prototype analytics into benchmarked evidence (the `usability-analytics` canon); feeds `product-designer` |
| `consumer-migrator` | CONSUMER file(s) (instance swaps + override re-application) | propagating a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish across consumers — runs the `rebind` procedure; confirms changes are consumed |

**Mental model:** `product-designer` deconstructs the ask + defines the right thing (business goal + why +
what) → *optionally* `art-director` sets the on-brand visual direction (adapt a reference, never copy) →
`ui-designer` builds it right (compose {{SYSTEM_NAME}}, pixel fidelity + system compliance) → the screens are
**usability-validated via a coded prototype** by `product-designer` against the business goal AND CX → the
**validated** screens hand off to product + engineering / go live. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found mid-build routes to
the **DS context** (`ds-steward` / `component-designer`) → they tokenize/build/publish → this context
consumes the published result.

