## Roster

| Agent | Owns | Fires on |
|---|---|---|
| `product-designer` | intake/requirements deconstruction (business goal · metric · segment · JTBD · constraints · scope · CX criteria), flows, IA, state matrices, interaction/a11y specs, research synthesis, acceptance criteria, functional microcopy, the usability-validation gate | "deconstruct these requirements", "turn this PRD/brief into a design brief", "what business goal does this serve", "plan the UX for X", "map the flow", "what states does this need", "write the spec", "synthesize this research", "what should this error/empty state say" |
| `art-director` *(optional)* | creative direction from a reference/trend — deconstruct → filter through the token/brand fence → adapt-not-copy → 2–3 named directions → low-fi `Explorations` → build spec (the `visual-craft` canon) | "recreate this screen with a fresh take", "make it look like [app] but on-brand", "give me creative directions / layout options", "what trend fits this screen", "explore visual options", "clean it up / make it more aesthetic" |
| `ui-designer` | composing {{SYSTEM_NAME}} into pixel-perfect consumer screens, build-time design-review self-check, consumer-file drift sweep | "build/recreate the X screen", "compose this flow in Figma", "sweep the consumer file for drift" |
| `flow-reviewer` | INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation of screens + flows (the `ux-flow-review` canon) | "review this screen/flow", "heuristic evaluation", "is this usable / AA-compliant", "evaluate this journey" |
| `data-analyst` | turning prototype analytics into screen-validation evidence (the `usability-analytics` canon) | "analyze the usability data", "what does the data say", "benchmark SEQ / task success / time-on-task", "where are users dropping off" |
| `consumer-migrator` | propagating a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish across consumer files (the `rebind` procedure) | "migrate the consumer onto the new X", "the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} update shipped — sweep the consumer", "confirm the publish is consumed" |

**Shared building blocks** — reusable pieces every relevant role loads, so behavior never drifts:
- **`ux-flow-review` skill** = the single heuristic-evaluation canon (5 frameworks + {{DOMAIN}} + WCAG
  2.2 AA). `ui-designer` (self-check), `flow-reviewer` (gate), `/design-review` all load it.
- **`visual-craft` skill** = the creative-direction canon (deconstruct → filter through the token/brand
  fence → adapt-not-copy → 2–3 named directions → low-fi Explorations). `art-director` runs it;
  `/art-direction` delegates to it. Aesthetics never overrides usability/a11y; a new-component need is a DS gap.
- **`usability-analytics` skill** = the empirical-validation canon (metrics + UX benchmarks +
  triangulation + stats caution). `data-analyst` runs it; `product-designer` validates against its verdicts.
  Expert review + empirical data are complementary, not redundant.
- **`rebind` skill** = the consume-verification procedure. `consumer-migrator` runs it across files.
- **`flow-layout` skill** = section/frame auto-layout by flow name (place-new + re-flow). `ui-designer`
  runs it via `/relayout`.
- **`figma-versioning` skill** (★ cross-cutting, **no agent of its own**) = named version-history
  checkpoints on the consumer file, folded into `ui-designer` (`pre-build:` / `gate-pass:`),
  `consumer-migrator` (`pre-rebind:` — before the instance swap, the load-bearing one), and
  `art-director` (before writing Explorations); invoked directly via `/checkpoint` + `/changelog`.

**Quality gate (the delivery seam)** — `ui-designer` builds incrementally, render-verifying each
phase, then runs **two Figma gates at delivery**: the **design-review self-check** (its build-time
application of the `ux-flow-review` canon — zero blockers) AND the **Gotcha #27 binding audit** on any
new frame built outside {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instances — zero unbound. Then **`flow-reviewer` runs the same canon
independently** as the usability gate (a fresh evaluator catches what the builder rationalized away).
A screen is not done until all pass.

**Usability-validation gate (required, before handoff).** The Figma gates verify *fidelity +
compliance*; they do not prove the design *works for users*. So every flow bound for product +
engineering is first **usability-tested as a coded prototype** (`usability-prototype`) — cohort
separation, Clarity heatmaps, PostHog time-on-task, post-task SEQ. `product-designer` owns this gate and
runs it against the business goal AND the CX success criteria. Task success / time-on-task / SEQ must
clear before handoff; a failure routes back to `product-designer` / `ui-designer`, not forward. This is a
gate, not an optional extra — designs do not go live or reach engineers unvalidated.

