## Slash commands (thin wrappers — they delegate, they don't duplicate)

| Command | Delegates to | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `/design-review [screen / flow / node-id]` | `flow-reviewer` | independent heuristic evaluation (the `ux-flow-review` canon) |
| `/consumer-audit [page / "all"]` | `ui-designer` | sweep the consumer file for drift + migration opportunities |
| `/art-direction [screen / flow / reference / trend]` | `art-director` (runs `visual-craft`) | creative visual directions from a reference/trend — on-brand, inside {{SYSTEM_NAME}} |
| `/rebind [component / file / "all"]` | `consumer-migrator` | migrate consumer instances onto a freshly published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} main |
| `/usability-report [screen / flow / "pilot"]` | `data-analyst` | analyze prototype analytics into validation evidence (vs UX benchmarks) |
| `/relayout [flow / page / "all"]` | `ui-designer` (runs `flow-layout`) | auto-lay screens into sized, named sections grouped by flow (place-new + re-flow) |
| `/checkpoint [label / "pre-build" / "pre-rebind" / "milestone"]` | `figma-versioning` skill | save a named version-history restore point on the consumer file |
| `/changelog [version range / "latest"]` | `figma-versioning` skill | list / diff consumer-file versions + generate a changelog between two points |

Each command body only *invokes the agent* — the workflow lives in **one** place. If a command
restates the lens, the same workflow now exists twice and keeping them in sync is the exact drift
problem this repo exists to kill. Add new commands the same way: thin, delegating — never duplicate.

